📋 5. FULL PACKAGE — READY TO PUSH

Step 1 — Create the repository

Go to github.com/new:

· Name : nexus-w3c-validator
· Description : 🌐 NEXUS W3C Validator — Multi-Standard Code Validator (HTML5, CSS, RDF, i18n, Feed, EPUB)
· Public : ✅
· Initialize with README : ❌ (we'll add it)

Step 2 — Push the files

```bash
cd ~/nexus-w3c-validator
git init
git add nexus_w3c_validator.py README.md .gitignore
git commit -m "🌐 NEXUS W3C Validator v1.0.0 — 8 W3C standards, 0 dependencies"
git remote add origin https://github.com/Aissamohammedi88/nexus-w3c-validator.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

Step 3 — Add topics on GitHub

In Settings → Topics, add:

```
w3c-validator
html5-validator
css-validator
rdf-validator
i18n-checker
epubcheck
feed-validator
web-standards
code-validation
developer-tools
python
localhost
self-hosted
nexus
open-source
```

